  "text": "Dr. Kebede Michael (November 2, 1916 – November 12, 1998) was one of the most prolific and versatile Ethiopian intellectuals, authors, and poets of the 20th century. Over a career spanning several decades, he authored or translated around 90 published works. His diverse bibliography spans school textbooks, poetry, plays, history, philosophy, and socio-economic development. Early"
